    <string name="onboarding_1_title">Welcome to SyncMesh</string>
    <string name="onboarding_1_desc">Your devices, one clipboard. SyncMesh links the phones around you into a private local mesh — fast, offline, and under your control.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_title">What SyncMesh does</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_desc">Copy on one device, paste on another. SyncMesh keeps a searchable history of everything shared, and future updates will add file and image transfer over the same mesh.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_title">Permissions, explained</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_desc">Notifications keep the sync service visible while it runs in the background. Camera is used only when you scan a pairing QR code. Nothing else is requested.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_4_title">How clipboard sync works</string>
    <string name="onboarding_4_desc">Tap Start Sync on each device. Whenever you copy text, SyncMesh sends it directly to your paired devices over Wi-Fi — there is no server in the middle.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_5_title">Pairing your devices</string>
    <string name="onboarding_5_desc">Every device shows a 6-digit pairing code. Scan the QR code, tap a nearby device, or type an IP address — whichever is easiest. Pair once, sync forever.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_6_title">The keyboard add-on</string>
    <string name="onboarding_6_desc">Android 10+ blocks background clipboard access. Enable the bundled SyncMesh keyboard and your clipboard is sent reliably the moment you start typing.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_7_title">Private by design</string>
    <string name="onboarding_7_desc">No account. No cloud. No analytics. Your clipboard never leaves your local network, and history is stored only on this device.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_8_title">You\'re ready</string>
    <string name="onboarding_8_desc">Start the sync service, pair your first device, and copy something. A short tour will show you around the app.</string>

